
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@courseId = 1
@moduleId = 1

# ---- LOGIN (OAuth 2.0 device flow against Keycloak, as a third-party client) ----
# Keycloak must be running (docker compose up keycloak).
# A. Send request A, open "verification_uri_complete" from the response in a browser
#    and log in (e.g. teacher / KEYCLOAK_DEMO_PASSWORD from .env).
# B. Then send request B. Every request below uses its access token via {{token}}.
# The token lives 5 minutes; when you get 401, run A and B again.
# The user must be on the LMS class list (request C in content.http imports the demo users).

@keycloakUrl = http://localhost:8081/realms/lms/protocol/openid-connect
@token = {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}
# lms-cli requires PKCE, also in the device flow. A fixed pair is fine for this
# development file: the device flow is protected by the user's approval in the browser.
@pkceVerifier = lms-http-client-dev-only-verifier-0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuv
@pkceChallenge = 1gtkZbQDSQppQudg22Jeydpbypl4KzjRT0GF1ZCsWVc

### A. Start login (device flow)
# @name device
POST {{keycloakUrl}}/auth/device
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=lms-cli&scope=openid&code_challenge={{pkceChallenge}}&code_challenge_method=S256

### B. Fetch the access token (after logging in in the browser)
# @name login
POST {{keycloakUrl}}/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=lms-cli&grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code&device_code={{device.response.body.$.device_code}}&code_verifier={{pkceVerifier}}

### C. Import the demo users (log in as admin in A/B first; expect 200 with a report per row)
# Creates LMS profiles only: the users then register in Keycloak themselves with the
# same email. Safe to repeat: existing emails are reported as ALREADY_EXISTS.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/import
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=LmsBoundary

--LmsBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="demo-users.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ../../infra/demo-users.csv
--LmsBoundary--

### 1. List course modules
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/{{courseId}}/modules
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2. Create StaticPage
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/{{courseId}}/modules/{{moduleId}}/contents/pages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Introduction to Java",
  "position": 0,
  "body": "Java is an object-oriented programming language."
}

### 3. List content summaries
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/{{courseId}}/modules/{{moduleId}}/contents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Test invalid request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/{{courseId}}/modules/{{moduleId}}/contents/pages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "position": -1,
  "body": ""
}

### 5. Test wrong Course ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/999999/modules/{{moduleId}}/contents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


@contentId = 5

### 6. Get StaticPage detail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/contents/{{contentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Get nonexistent StaticPage
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/contents/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}